version: "1.0.0"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   <- filled in after Zenodo mints it (docs/RELEASE.md)
repository-code: "https://github.com/Major-Project-Amrita/Cooperative-payload-transport-by-a-four-robot-formation"
keywords:
  - multi-robot systems
  - cooperative transport
  - local planning
  - benchmark
  - replication
  - MuJoCo
  - ROS 2
abstract: >-
  An open, replicated benchmark of ten local steering laws (APF, VFH, FGM, DWA,
  lattice MPC, MPPI, three histogram variants and a learned DAgger policy) for a
  team of differential-drive robots carrying one rigid payload through
  warehouses with moving traffic. Two independent implementations (MATLAB and
  Python/ROS 2) agree step for step at zero noise; the evaluation randomises
  the traffic phase per run, tunes every planner under an equal budget, varies
  team size and warehouse layout, separates ground-truth collision screening
  from a deployable sensor-based safety monitor, and validates in MuJoCo
  physics. Simulation only.
